<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <POU Name="AssertionBase" Id="{bb18ca78-e6ef-448f-a67d-ba9d44a932c6}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[{region 'Documentation'}
(*!
<summary>Shared cyclic assertion lifecycle, identity and monotonic result escalation.</summary>
<description>

Initialize from the owning Test Case configuration, then call the concrete FB once per
cycle with its typed inputs. Derived FB bodies call SUPER^() once. The base invokes Assert only
after successful initialization and outside a reset call.

Enable controls observation. ObserveFirstCycle determines whether its first enabled call
is observed. EvaluationActive normally follows ObservationActive; explicit-evaluation and
history-based families refine this gate.

Reset queues work for the next FB call: result becomes NotEvaluated, observation history
is cleared by ResetAssertion and that call performs no assertion check. Identity and publisher
binding are retained. Initialize also queues this reset, including when initialization
fails.

Pass cannot clear Failed or Error. Fail escalates NotEvaluated or Passed; Error can also
escalate Failed. Findings are published once per result escalation, not every cyclic failure. A
failed publication is not retried.

State is owner-supplied finding context, not a state machine input. Diagnostic value text
may be shortened or rounded; comparisons use the original typed values. The selected publisher
must exist before any publication.

</description>
*)
{endregion}
FUNCTION_BLOCK ABSTRACT AssertionBase IMPLEMENTS I_Assertion
VAR_INPUT
    Enable : BOOL; //! Enables observation; Initialize's ObserveFirstCycle setting controls the first enabled call.
    State : E_State := E_State.Uninitialized; //! Owner's current lifecycle state included in finding events; default Uninitialized.
END_VAR
VAR
    /// Instance binding selected by BindPublisher or lazily by EventPublisher.
    FEventPublisher : I_EventPublisher;
    FName : STRING(GVL_Constants.NameLength) := '<UnnamedAssertion>';
    FResourceName : STRING(GVL_Constants.ResourceNameLength);
    FResult : E_Result := E_Result.NotEvaluated;
    FEnabled : BOOL;
    FInitialized : BOOL;
    FResetRequested : BOOL;
    FObserveFirstCycle : BOOL := TRUE;
    FEnablePrevious : BOOL;
    FResetActive : BOOL;
END_VAR]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[FEnablePrevious := FEnabled AND NOT FResetActive;
FEnabled := Enable;
FResetActive := FResetRequested;

IF FResetActive THEN
    FResetRequested := FALSE;
    FEnablePrevious := FALSE;
    FResult := E_Result.NotEvaluated;
    ResetAssertion();
    RETURN;
END_IF;

IF NOT FInitialized THEN
    RETURN;
END_IF;

Assert();]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
    <Folder Name="Internal" Id="{a1e41711-db90-43f9-a309-8807c87da49c}" />
    <Method Name="Assert" Id="{097e2057-2cc2-4538-b403-1a3cb7cca076}" FolderPath="Internal\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{region 'Documentation'}
(*!
<summary>Implement the typed observation and result check.</summary>
<description>

Called once per initialized non-reset FB call, including disabled calls. Apply the
family-specific ObservationActive and EvaluationActive gates. Validate prerequisites before
access; applicable Error checks precede Failed checks and Pass is the successful
fallback.

Do not suppress required observation or configuration-error checks merely because Result
is Failed. The implementation comment provides an illustrative ordering, not mandatory test
conditions.

</description>
*)
{endregion}
METHOD PROTECTED ABSTRACT Assert]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[(*
Implementation sketch, not a mandatory copy template.
Keep applicable Error checks before Failed checks; Pass is the fallback.
Omit conditions that do not exist. Multiple branches per severity are allowed.

Before result evaluation:
- Perform required observation/snapshot work under its own activity gate.
- Validate each operation's prerequisites before accessing its data.
- Observation errors may occur without EvaluationActive.
- Do not skip required observation or memory safety checks because of Result.
- Validate independent initialization/configuration when it is performed;
  do not report unused inputs as errors merely because the FB is called.

Example result evaluation (placeholder conditions/messages):

IF NOT EvaluationActive THEN
    RETURN;
END_IF;

IF Result = E_Result.Error THEN
    RETURN;
END_IF;

IF ErrorConditionA THEN
    Error(Message := ErrorMessageA);
    RETURN;
END_IF;

IF ErrorConditionB THEN
    Error(Message := ErrorMessageB);
    RETURN;
END_IF;

IF Result = E_Result.Failed THEN
    RETURN;
END_IF;

IF FailureConditionA THEN
    Fail(Message := FailureMessageA);
    RETURN;
END_IF;

IF FailureConditionB THEN
    Fail(Message := FailureMessageB);
    RETURN;
END_IF;

Pass();

A held Failed result must not bypass applicable Error checks.
Pass/Fail/Error retain the monotonic result and suppress repeated findings.
*)]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="BindPublisher" Id="{ed1d5b65-3246-4d4c-b8e5-04b552c23001}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{region 'Documentation'}
(*!
<summary>Select the instance publisher immediately; ignore a zero assignment.</summary>
<description>

Retains identity, result and observation state. The caller owns the service lifetime.
There is no lifecycle guard, reset or replay when replacing this binding.

</description>
*)
{endregion}
METHOD PUBLIC BindPublisher
VAR_INPUT
    Publisher : I_EventPublisher; //! Publisher retained by the Assertion; caller owns its lifetime. Zero leaves the current binding unchanged.
END_VAR]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[IF Publisher = 0 THEN
    RETURN;
END_IF;

FEventPublisher := Publisher;]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Property Name="Enabled" Id="{05b19444-832b-4f39-86e4-1668f2ef156d}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{region 'Documentation'}
(*!
<summary>Enable accepted at the last FB call; not proof of evaluation.</summary>
*)
{endregion}
{attribute 'monitoring' := 'call'}
PROPERTY PUBLIC Enabled : BOOL //! Enable accepted at the last FB call; not proof of evaluation.]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{f7f72a83-f06f-46cc-90ff-ca3ba5f16c4d}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[PUBLIC]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[Enabled := FEnabled;]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Method Name="Error" Id="{7efa3286-0c2e-45da-8099-51fb5fa25530}" FolderPath="Internal\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{region 'Documentation'}
(*!
<summary>Escalate any non-Error result to Error and publish one finding.</summary>
<description>

Failed can escalate to Error. Repeated Error calls do nothing. The result is stored
before publication; a publication failure is not retried.

</description>
*)
{endregion}
METHOD PROTECTED Error
VAR_INPUT
    Message : STRING(GVL_Constants.MessageLength); //! Diagnostic text for this finding; copied into the event within MessageLength.
END_VAR
VAR
    Finding : ST_Event;
    PublishResult : INT;
END_VAR]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[IF FResult = E_Result.Error THEN
    RETURN;
END_IF;

FResult := E_Result.Error;
Finding := CreateAssertionErrorEvent(Name := FName,
    ResourceName := FResourceName,
    State := State,
    Message := Message);
PublishResult := EventPublisher.PublishEvent(Event := Finding);]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Property Name="EvaluationActive" Id="{66689336-414c-42ab-925b-96c52f7dcb40}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{region 'Documentation'}
(*!
<summary>Use the polymorphic ObservationActive gate for direct result evaluation.</summary>
<description>

Explicit-evaluation and history-based descendants override this getter. A TRUE gate
permits checking; it does not mean the result is Passed or that this call has published a
finding.

</description>
*)
{endregion}
{attribute 'monitoring' := 'call'}
PROPERTY PUBLIC EvaluationActive : BOOL //! Effective gate for direct result evaluation; delegates to ObservationActive in this base.]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{e480abf5-bbb8-4928-aafd-92b8915a77e4}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[PUBLIC]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[EvaluationActive := ObservationActive;]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Property Name="EventPublisher" Id="{39d78fff-4328-428c-94cc-af4d3d7b0c05}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{region 'Documentation'}
(*!
<summary>Return the instance publisher, binding the global default lazily if still
unset.</summary>
<description>

The first read without a local binding copies GVL_EventBuffer.Publisher. A nonzero local
binding is retained; later global changes do not replace it. This getter can therefore change
the binding. Publication requires a valid publisher.

</description>
*)
{endregion}
{attribute 'monitoring' := 'variable'}
PROPERTY PUBLIC EventPublisher : I_EventPublisher //! Instance publisher; the first unbound access adopts and retains the global default.]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{eaaf9709-6837-41fa-b249-c4a5494a5b04}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[PUBLIC]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[IF FEventPublisher = 0 THEN
    FEventPublisher := GVL_EventBuffer.Publisher;
END_IF;
EventPublisher := FEventPublisher;]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Method Name="Fail" Id="{1eb6f02e-b2e0-493a-a0b2-777c39345d18}" FolderPath="Internal\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{region 'Documentation'}
(*!
<summary>Escalate NotEvaluated or Passed to Failed and publish one finding.</summary>
<description>

Already Failed or Error is unchanged. The result is stored before publication; a
publication failure is not retried.

</description>
*)
{endregion}
METHOD PROTECTED Fail
VAR_INPUT
    Message : STRING(GVL_Constants.MessageLength); //! Diagnostic text for this finding; copied into the event within MessageLength.
END_VAR
VAR
    Finding : ST_Event;
    PublishResult : INT;
END_VAR]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[CASE FResult OF
    E_Result.NotEvaluated, E_Result.Passed:
        FResult := E_Result.Failed;
ELSE
    RETURN;
END_CASE;

Finding := CreateAssertionFailedEvent(Name := FName,
    ResourceName := FResourceName,
    State := State,
    Message := Message);
PublishResult := EventPublisher.PublishEvent(Event := Finding);]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="Initialize" Id="{18d24ef9-99d2-4ccd-a916-129c986db101}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{region 'Documentation'}
(*!
<summary>Configure the hierarchical identity and observation settings; return initialization
success.</summary>
<description>
The Parent Test Case identity must already be valid. The complete name consists of the
Parent's three hierarchy segments and a nonempty local Assertion suffix, which may contain
additional dots. It must fit NameLength; sibling uniqueness remains the caller's
responsibility. The parent interface is read here, not retained.
The composed name is length-limited into Name before validation of the unshortened name,
so an invalid name can remain available for diagnostics. Missing parent or invalid name
publishes a framework error and returns FALSE.
Clears base result and enable history and queues ResetAssertion for the next FB call,
where typed inputs are bound. ResourceName and ObserveFirstCycle are copied after a parent is
available. TRUE enables subsequent checking; normal Reset retains these settings.
</description>
*)
{endregion}
METHOD PUBLIC FINAL Initialize : BOOL //! TRUE after successful identity and setup validation; FALSE leaves the object uninitialized.
VAR_INPUT
    Parent : I_TestCase; //! Owning Test Case with an established Name; read during initialization, not retained.
    AssertionName : STRING(GVL_Constants.NameLength); //! Nonempty assertion suffix appended to Parent.Name; the complete name must satisfy the naming contract.
    ResourceName : STRING(GVL_Constants.ResourceNameLength) := ''; //! Optional resource context copied into finding events; empty by default.
    ObserveFirstCycle : BOOL := TRUE; //! TRUE observes the first enabled call; FALSE skips it. Default TRUE; does not delay explicit Evaluate.
END_VAR
VAR
    ParentName : STRING(GVL_Constants.NameLength);
    FullName : STRING(2 * GVL_Constants.NameLength + 1);
END_VAR]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[Initialize := FALSE;
FInitialized := FALSE;
FResult := E_Result.NotEvaluated;
FEnabled := FALSE;
FEnablePrevious := FALSE;
FResetRequested := TRUE;
FResetActive := TRUE;

IF Parent = 0 THEN
    EventPublisher.PublishEvent(Event := CreateFrameworkEvent(Name := AssertionName,
        ResourceName := ResourceName,
        State := E_State.Uninitialized,
        Severity := E_EventSeverity.Error,
        Message := 'Missing Test Case parent.'));
    RETURN;
END_IF;

ParentName := Parent.Name;
FullName := CONCAT(CONCAT(ParentName, '.'), AssertionName);
// SA0175: ASCII name contract; byte-based access is intentional and bounded.
{analysis -175}
FName := LEFT(FullName, UINT_TO_INT(GVL_Constants.NameLength));
{analysis +175}
FResourceName := ResourceName;
FObserveFirstCycle := ObserveFirstCycle;

IF NOT IsNameValid(Name := FullName, Depth := 4) THEN
    EventPublisher.PublishEvent(Event := CreateFrameworkEvent(Name := FName,
        ResourceName := FResourceName,
        State := E_State.Uninitialized,
        Severity := E_EventSeverity.Error,
        Message := CONCAT('Invalid Assertion name: ', FullName)));
    RETURN;
END_IF;

FInitialized := TRUE;
Initialize := TRUE;]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Property Name="IsInitialized" Id="{18d24ef9-99d2-4ccd-a916-129c986db103}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{region 'Documentation'}
(*!
<summary>TRUE after successful explicit initialization; retained by normal Reset.</summary>
*)
{endregion}
{attribute 'monitoring' := 'call'}
PROPERTY PUBLIC IsInitialized : BOOL //! TRUE after successful explicit initialization; retained by normal Reset.]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{18d24ef9-99d2-4ccd-a916-129c986db104}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[PUBLIC]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[IsInitialized := FInitialized;]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Property Name="Name" Id="{c5d91f87-9cf8-4606-b3fd-111ae5728898}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{region 'Documentation'}
(*!
<summary>Length-limited hierarchical event name assigned by Initialize; retained by
Reset.</summary>
<description>

May contain an invalid diagnostic name; IsInitialized indicates validity.

</description>
*)
{endregion}
{attribute 'monitoring' := 'variable'}
PROPERTY PUBLIC Name : STRING(GVL_Constants.NameLength) //! Length-limited hierarchical event name assigned by Initialize; retained by Reset.]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{51a7b121-0be7-4b4c-bd40-2e30d5b80251}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[PUBLIC]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[Name := FName;]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Property Name="ObservationActive" Id="{834f1dbf-86c1-4c3e-8e3b-a9948589f4a7}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{region 'Documentation'}
(*!
<summary>Indicate whether observation is enabled for the current accepted FB inputs.</summary>
<description>

Requires successful initialization, no reset in this call and Enabled. With
ObserveFirstCycle FALSE, a preceding enabled non-reset call is required. Overrides preserve
reset suppression and remain side-effect-free.

</description>
*)
{endregion}
{attribute 'monitoring' := 'call'}
PROPERTY PUBLIC ObservationActive : BOOL //! TRUE when initialized and enabled outside Reset, subject to the first-cycle setting and accepted call history.]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{c7d84758-0103-4ebf-baf3-28cd4910f991}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[PUBLIC]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[ObservationActive := FInitialized AND NOT FResetActive AND FEnabled
    AND (FObserveFirstCycle OR FEnablePrevious);]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Property Name="ObserveFirstCycle" Id="{60901a72-0430-4f18-9d15-ff34e332ef4d}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{region 'Documentation'}
(*!
<summary>Read-only first-cycle setting supplied through Initialize; default TRUE, retained by
Reset.</summary>
<description>

Initialize with FALSE when the commanded test object must process before
observation.

</description>
*)
{endregion}
{attribute 'monitoring' := 'call'}
PROPERTY PUBLIC ObserveFirstCycle : BOOL //! Read-only first-cycle setting supplied through Initialize; default TRUE, retained by Reset.]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{ae229a2e-b117-4c86-bbaa-cabef22b3d8c}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[PUBLIC]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[ObserveFirstCycle := FObserveFirstCycle;]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Method Name="Pass" Id="{00113c93-312b-4b7e-a5db-69d6a0327a3e}" FolderPath="Internal\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{region 'Documentation'}
(*!
<summary>Promote NotEvaluated to Passed without publishing a finding.</summary>
<description>

Leaves Passed, Failed and Error unchanged.

</description>
*)
{endregion}
METHOD PROTECTED Pass]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[IF FResult = E_Result.NotEvaluated THEN
    FResult := E_Result.Passed;
END_IF;]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="Reset" Id="{ec54424c-7436-45d1-a5d7-8457ff73de04}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{region 'Documentation'}
(*!
<summary>Request a reset to be consumed by the next FB call.</summary>
<description>

Does not immediately change Result. The consuming call clears result and observation
state and returns without checking; typed FB inputs must be bound for family-specific reset
work. Identity, settings and publisher are retained.

</description>
*)
{endregion}
METHOD PUBLIC Reset]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[FResetRequested := TRUE;]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="ResetAssertion" Id="{98959708-35bc-4a02-ae53-b28ef33acb67}" FolderPath="Internal\">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{region 'Documentation'}
(*!
<summary>Reset family-specific observation state while FB inputs are bound.</summary>
<description>

The base implementation is empty. Override for owned history, snapshots or counters; do
not publish findings here. Called by the reset FB path, never directly by Initialize.

</description>
*)
{endregion}
METHOD PROTECTED ResetAssertion]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Property Name="ResourceName" Id="{21f10956-ded2-48db-8c2d-92cbdeeddd41}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{region 'Documentation'}
(*!
<summary>Read-only tested resource context supplied through Initialize; default '', retained by
Reset.</summary>
*)
{endregion}
{attribute 'monitoring' := 'variable'}
PROPERTY PUBLIC ResourceName : STRING(GVL_Constants.ResourceNameLength) //! Read-only tested resource context supplied through Initialize; default '', retained by Reset.]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{855a72e0-5a00-4ef3-9ff6-c14025ca6069}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[PUBLIC]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[ResourceName := FResourceName;]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Property Name="Result" Id="{35612613-f714-46ff-9182-8889ea8ff1f0}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{region 'Documentation'}
(*!
<summary>Return the held assertion result.</summary>
<description>

Passed, Failed and Error do not de-escalate during checking. Consuming Reset or calling
Initialize clears the result to NotEvaluated. Disabled calls alone do not clear it.

</description>
*)
{endregion}
{attribute 'monitoring' := 'call'}
PROPERTY PUBLIC Result : E_Result //! Held assertion result; ordinary evaluation cannot lower Failed or Error.]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{3593cda1-f260-4f0f-80bd-645c3a2fba63}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[PUBLIC]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[Result := FResult;]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>